# Pairs with NoLostWrite. The covering check trusts the earliest export with a
# cut without requiring every later export to have one, so the echo of a later
# export taken off the purge hold settles the gap and the rewind skips writes
# that export does not hold. It perturbs the covering-check definition, not
# an action.
MODULE: NoLostWriteCoveringRunNotContiguous
TARGET: NoLostWrite
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the covering export run need not be contiguous, so an untrusted later bootstrap settles the gap

--- FIND
Covers(k) == \A j \in k..epoch : cut[j] # NoCut /\ trim <= cut[j]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only export k itself must carry a cut.
Covers(k) == cut[k] # NoCut /\ trim <= cut[k]
--- END